# Gradle leaves its build cache inside android/ — lock files, checksum databases
# and compiled .class files. These patterns do NOT hold on their own: when
# package.json has a `files` allowlist, naming a directory in it wins over an
# ignore rule for a path inside that directory, so `android` in `files` shipped
# android/build/ regardless of what was written here. The allowlist now names
# `android/build.gradle` and `android/src` instead, which is what actually keeps
# build output out of the tarball. Kept as defence in depth.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/local.properties
ios/build/
